        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>From discussions elsewhere it would appear Surprise Shift is available to use regardless of what Form you’re in.  However, Change Form is only available when in your Base Form.  It still should be clarified further otherwise Surprise Shift does seem outright worse.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That would be a reason for it, then. And yeah, if that’s the case, it really needs to be clarified.</p>",
